.TH TERMCODE 1 "2026" "termcode" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termcode \- a VS Code-style code editor and Git panel in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termcode
.RB [ \-\-tab ]
.RI [ path [: line [: column ]]]
.br
.B termcode
.BR \-\-default\-config " | " \-V " | " \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termcode
opens a folder, a file or a git repository in the terminal it is started in, the way
.B code
does in a window: a file Explorer, Search, Source Control with a commit graph, tabs and
split editors, side\-by\-side diffs, a minimap, Go to Definition and VS Code themes.
Quitting returns the terminal to the shell.
It has no language server and runs no extensions: definitions and references are found
by searching the code with
.BR rg (1).
.PP
Without a
.IR path ,
it opens the git repository the current folder is in, or the folder itself.
A folder becomes the workspace root; Source Control still covers its whole repository.
A file opens at
.I line
and
.I column
when they are given, with its repository (or its folder) as the root.
Relative paths resolve against the current folder; a name starting with
.B \-
needs
.BR ./ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tab
Open in a
.B Code
tab of the current herdr workspace instead (reused when one is open for that root).
Also used when there is no terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-config
Print the default settings file: every option of the Settings window, commented out
at its default.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.SH KEYS
Press
.B F1
for every command and its key. Some to start with:
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open a file by name;
.B :42
goes to a line,
.B @
to a function.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S\fR, \fBCtrl+W\fR, \fBCtrl+Q
Save, close the tab, quit (each asks about unsaved changes).
.TP
.B Ctrl+F\fR, \fBCtrl+H
Find, replace.
.TP
.B F12
Go to Definition.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+`
Show or hide the terminal: your
.B $SHELL
under the editors. It takes every key but Ctrl+`, F1 and Ctrl+Q, and the terminal keys:
Ctrl+Shift+` opens another shell (each gets a tab on the panel's border), Ctrl+PgUp and
Ctrl+PgDn switch between them, and Ctrl+F at the shell's prompt finds text in the scrollback.
.TP
.B Explorer
Ctrl+click, Shift+click or Shift+Up/Down select several items; a drag moves them (with
Ctrl or Alt held as it ends: copies them), Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X and Ctrl+V copy and move them,
Delete moves them to the Trash and Shift+Delete deletes them; Ctrl+Z takes back all but
Shift+Delete. Esc stops a paste that is still copying. Resting the pointer on a file shows its
MD5, with a button that copies it.
.TP
.B Binary files
A file with a NUL byte near its start, or any
.BR .bin ,
opens as a read-only hexdump, as
.B hexdump \-C
prints it; F1
.B View: Toggle Hexdump
shows it as text instead, or any file as a hexdump.
.PP
Any F1 command can have a key of your own: see
.B termcode.keybindings
below.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/termcode/settings.json
Settings, in VS Code's format (comments allowed). Written on the first start, listing
every option at its default. Keys include
.BR termcode.icons ,
.BR termcode.colors ,
.BR termcode.keybindings ,
.B termcode.errorChecking
and
.BR workbench.colorTheme .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/termcode/
Sessions, layout, backups of unsaved files, commit drafts and trusted repositories.
.PP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
and
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
move these, as they do for other programs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMCODE_ICONS
.BR nerd ,
.B unicode
or
.B ascii
.RB ( 0
is ascii): which icons to draw, over the setting.
.TP
.B TERMCODE_COLORS
.BR truecolor ,
.B 256
or
.BR 16 :
the terminal's colours, over the setting.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM
Read to pick the colour depth and icons when nothing sets them.
.SH SECURITY
A repository whose own git settings make git run a program while reading it
(core.fsmonitor, diff.external, textconv, filters) gets no git command until you trust
it in Source Control. A project's compile_commands.json never runs a program of its
own: only a compiler found on
.B PATH
by name, with flags that only shape how code is read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal quit; 1 when the path does not exist or the options are wrong.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at
.UR https://github.com/JonasAtelier/termcode\-releases/issues
.UE ;
in termcode,
.B F1 Help: Report Issue
copies what a report needs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR rg (1),
.BR shellcheck (1)
